 `loading: 'text-pages'` and `'bytes-complete'` use the shared file reader. With `'renderer'`, the selected body mounts before any bytes are read and receives `content: { kind: 'renderer', revision, loaded, failed, reload }`. Its injected face owns content loading, errors, store updates, and cancellation. `loaded(version)` records the displayed source version and ends loading. `failed()` ends loading without recording a successful version, allowing a later file change to retry; reports from replaced revisions are ignored. `reload()` increments the revision, which the body observes to cancel and replace its request. The body also cancels on unmount and tab closure, retains settled content in its declared tab store, and releases that state when the tab ends. [Office previews](#office-preview) use this mode without putting converted bytes or font metadata in the shared file store.
 
+<a id="reusable-preview"></a>
+## Reusable preview
+
+Unrelated UI parents render the root-scoped `document.preview` Factory through `renderFactorySlot('document.preview', { fileName, read, renderOffice?, revision?, failureText? })`. No Session or Sidebar tab is required. `read(signal)` returns `{ data: Uint8Array<ArrayBuffer>, mediaType? }`; the source owner enforces authorization and complete-file size limits on every read. For Word and PowerPoint suffixes, the Factory calls `renderOffice(signal)` instead of `read`, allowing an authorized provider to defer reading until admission to the shared [Office converter](../../document/office-to-pdf/README.md). Its result contains PDF bytes and optional `missingFonts`. Changing the filename, reader, conversion callback, or revision aborts the old operation and clears its bytes; closing the occurrence or unloading the plugin also cancels it. A failed replacement never keeps old contents visible. The default error is fixed localized copy; `failureText(error)` may return a source-specific public explanation.
+
+The Factory selects implementations from the same `documentPreviews` registry and reuses the native PDF, Excel, image, Markdown, code, plain-text, and sanitized static HTML renderers. Extensions that serve both entry points register a root-scoped `document.preview.body` under their registry id in addition to the Sidebar body. Its inputs are `fileName`, `content`, `signal`, `wrap`, and `scrollportRef`, without Session or file-resource hooks. Source text is decoded as complete UTF-8 and invalid or NUL-containing text is rejected. HTML never executes scripts or reads related files, and Markdown has no local file resolver. Viewing preferences live only in the mounted occurrence; the source owner supplies refresh and does not persist bytes in Session history.
+
